-- title:
--   Places read at good points avoid the Igusa node set
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $q\ge 5$, $M'$ a nonzero natural number with $q\nmid M'$, and $A\subseteq\overline{\mathbf Q}$ a valuation subring with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ lies in the nonunits of $A$. Two function fields are in play: the geometric $j$-line field $C:=$ `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`, generated over the residue field $\kappa:=$ `ResidueField A` by the $q$-expansions `jqModC` and `jqNModC`, and the full-level field $\bar F:=$ `fieldBar q M'` $=$ `xHFunctionFieldBar (q^2*M') (levelH q M')`, an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbf Q}\subseteq$ `LaurentSeries` $\overline{\mathbf Q}$, together with its characteristic-$q$ counterpart $\bar C:=$ `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q^2*M') (levelH q M')`.
--
--   The data and hypotheses are the following.
--
--   *Supersingular places.* $W$ is a finite set of places of $C$ over $\kappa$, and `hW` says that $W$ consists exactly of the supersingular places `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`: the places $w$ that are rational, are affine geometric places, and satisfy $w.\mathrm{evalAt}(j_{\mathrm{geom}})\in$ `ssJSet q` $\kappa$.
--
--   *Constant reduction of the $j$-line field.* `hle` is the inclusion `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` $\le\bar F$. $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ on `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` with values in $C$: a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, a surjective residue homomorphism onto $C$ with kernel the maximal ideal, inducing $A\to\kappa$ on constants, together with a degree-preserving map on places compatible with orders of functions. The hypothesis `hR₀` says that the reduction is the termwise one on integral Laurent series: for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose image in `LaurentSeries` $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that image lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   *Igusa components.* $\zeta$ is a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ (an element of `Idx q`), and $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ assigns a valuation subring of $\bar F$ to each point of $\mathbf P^1(\mathbf F_q)$, written [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21). The hypothesis `hIg_inf` identifies $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}($`lineInfty q`$)$, the ring attached to the point $(1:0)$, as a Gauss-type ring: $f$ belongs to it precisely when there are Laurent series $x,y$ over $A$ with the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ nonzero and $f\cdot y=x$ in `LaurentSeries` $\overline{\mathbf Q}$. The hypothesis `hIg` says that every point $L$ of $\mathbf P^1(\mathbf F_q)$ (the Lean binder is also named `ℓ`) is of the form $\mathrm{redQ}(\gamma)\cdot(1:0)$ for some $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ with $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(L)$ the pullback of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}((1:0))$ along `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`; `hIg_inj` says $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ is injective; `hIg_perm` says that for every root of unity $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ pulling back along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` permutes the family $\{O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(L)\}$.
--
--   *Drinfeld (supersingular) rings.* $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ assigns a valuation subring of $\bar F$ to each $s\in W$. `hSS_A` says that for $x\in\overline{\mathbf Q}$ the image of $x$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ iff $x\in A$. `hSS_over` says that for $s\in W$ and $f\in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ which is regular at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ at which the image of the $q$-expansion `jq` is regular, if the $R_0$-residue of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$, then the image of $f$ in $\bar F$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$, and for every $a\in A$ whose residue equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that $R_0$-residue the difference of the image of $f$ and the image of $a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$. `hSS_fix` says each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ is invariant under pullback along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` for all $\zeta'$ and all $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$. `hSS_tr` provides, for each $s$, an element $t\in O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ such that $t-a$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and is a unit there for every $a\in A$.
--
--   *Regular prolongation on the $\infty$-component.* $R$ is a `RegularProlongation` of $A$ on $\bar F$ with values in $\bar C$ (valuation subring, surjective residue map with kernel the maximal ideal, inducing $A\to\kappa$ on constants, and with every nonzero element scalable into the ring with nonzero residue), and `hR` identifies $R.\mathrm{integers}=O_{\mathrm{Ig}}((1:0))$. The hypothesis `hR₀O` says that $f$ lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ iff its image in $\bar F$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}((1:0))$.
--
--   *Constants.* $\pi\in\overline{\mathbf Q}$ satisfies $\pi^{q^2-1}=q$ and $\pi\in A$. $k_0$ is a subfield of $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ and $\pi_0\in k_0$ lies in $A$; the hypotheses `hdvr`, `hunif`, `hhens`, `hres` say that $A\cap k_0$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, henselian, with algebraically closed residue field, and `hκ` says every $a\in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$.
--
--   *Auxiliary prime data.* $\ell$ is a prime with $\ell\ge 3$, $\ell\neq q$ and $\ell\nmid M'$; $\zeta_0\in k_0$ is a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity; $\varpi_t\in k_0$ lies in $A$ and satisfies $\varpi_t^{q^2-1}=q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   *The finite layer.* $K_1$ is a finite extension of $k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ and $A_1$ a valuation subring of $K_1$ with $x\in A_1\iff x\in A$, assumed to be a henselian discrete valuation ring.
--
--   With $k_0$ acting on $\bar F$ through $\overline{\mathbf Q}$, the assertion quantifies over every intermediate field $F_0$ of $\bar F/k_0$ subject to four conditions: the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by all constants from $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ is all of $\bar F$; $F_0$ is stable under `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` for every $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; a linear-disjointness condition, namely for every finite extension $K'$ of $k_0$ in $\overline{\mathbf Q}$, every $m$, every $c:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to\overline{\mathbf Q}$ that is $K'$-linearly independent, and every family $a$ of elements of the compositum $T(K'):=k_0(\text{image of }K')\sqcup F_0$ with $\sum_i c_i\,a_i=0$, all $a_i$ vanish; and $F_0$ contains every element of $\bar F$ whose Laurent series has rational coefficients, i.e. lies in the range of `coeffEmb` $\overline{\mathbf Q}$.
--
--   Put $T_1:=$ `IntermediateField.adjoin k₀ (image of K₁ in F̄) ⊔ F₀`. The assertion further quantifies over an $A_1$-algebra structure on $T_1$ whose structure map is the inclusion on $A_1\subseteq K_1\subseteq\overline{\mathbf Q}\to\bar F$, over an element $j_1\in T_1$ whose image in $\bar F$ is the image under `hle` of the $q$-expansion `jq` of the modular invariant, assumed nonzero, and over a finite set $N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of places of $\bar C$ over $\kappa$ for which there exists a ring homomorphism $j:C\to\bar C$ such that (a) for every $f\in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ the image of $f$ in $\bar F$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R$-residue is $j$ applied to the $R_0$-residue of $f$, and (b) $Q\in N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ iff there is $s\in W$ with $g\in s.\mathrm{toValuationSubring}\iff j(g)\in Q.\mathrm{toValuationSubring}$ for all $g\in C$.
--
--   On the two-chart integral model $\mathfrak X:=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A₁ T₁ j₁`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout of $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the integral closures of $A_1[j_1]$ and $A_1[j_1^{-1}]$ in $T_1$ along their common middle chart, the statement introduces by `let`:
--
--   $\mathrm{InStalk}\,x\,f$: for every point $y$ of the finite chart `XFin` mapping to $x$ under `ιFin` there are $g,h$ in `chartAlgFin` with $h\notin y$ and $f\cdot h=g$ in $T_1$, and likewise for the chart at infinity; $\mathrm{InMax}\,x\,f$: the same with the additional requirement $g\in y$ in both clauses; $\mathrm{Centred}\,P\,x$, for a place $P$ of $\bar F$ over $\overline{\mathbf Q}$: $P$ is rational and every $f$ with $\mathrm{InStalk}\,x\,f$ is $P$-integral with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)\in A$ and with $A$-valuation $<1$ exactly when $\mathrm{InMax}\,x\,f$; $\mathrm{GoodPt}\,x$: the image of $x$ in $\mathrm{Spec}\,A_1$ is the closed point, $x$ admits no proper specialisation (every $y$ with $x\rightsquigarrow y$ equals $x$), every element of either chart algebra whose image in $\bar F$ lies in the nonunits of $R.\mathrm{integers}$ belongs to each prime of that chart above $x$, and for every $y$ in `XFin` above $x$, every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from `chartAlgFin` to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi($`jChartFin`$)$ is not in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7) $\Omega$; $\mathrm{Reads}\,x\,Q$, for a place $Q$ of $\bar C$: every $f$ with $\mathrm{InStalk}\,x\,f$ has its image in $R.\mathrm{integers}$, its $R$-residue lies in $Q.\mathrm{toValuationSubring}$, and that residue is a nonunit there exactly when $\mathrm{InMax}\,x\,f$; and $\mathrm{OffBranch}\,x$: for every point $L\neq(1:0)$ of $\mathbf P^1(\mathbf F_q)$ and every $y$ above $x$ in either chart there is an element of the corresponding chart algebra whose image in $\bar F$ lies in the nonunits of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(L)$ and which does not belong to $y$.
--
--   The conclusion is a single assertion: for every point $x$ of $\mathfrak X$ with $\mathrm{GoodPt}\,x$ and every place $Q$ of $\bar C$ over $\kappa$ with $\mathrm{Reads}\,x\,Q$, one has $Q\notin N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$. The predicates $\mathrm{Centred}$ and $\mathrm{OffBranch}$ are introduced in the statement but do not occur in this conclusion.
--
--   Within the construction of the semistable model of the full-level modular curve over a valuation ring above $q$, this records that a closed point of the special fibre which lies on the $\infty$-Igusa component and whose $j$-value is not supersingular reads a place of the reduced function field that is not one of the node places lying over the supersingular places of the $j$-line. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.reads_unique_and_exists_offBranch_of_not_mem_igusaNodes_twoChartIntegralModel`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.reads_unique_and_exists_offBranch_of_not_mem_igusaNodes_twoChartIntegralModel), where the residue discs of the Igusa base model are cut out by the points reading a given place.
